From dc42b9451b8f29542dd6fcb258111089eaa77b0f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hasan Mehdi <hasanthemehdi@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 10:15:41 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 07/15] erosqnative: robust HCI bring-up and H4 framing

- ACL/ISO length high byte was masked to zero ((x << 8) & 0xFF): any
  packet over 255 bytes desynced the stream (then panicked).
- Lost framing drops the byte and logs instead of panicking.
- REG_ON is cycled with the power-up delay, Launch_RAM gets its 250 ms,
  every init command is checked for Command Complete status with a
  timeout (no more hanging forever on a silent chip), one retry after a
  power cycle, and bt_hci_enable reports failure.
- The RX thread polls a stop flag so bt_hci_disable can join it.
- Simulator: without SDL threads there's no controller (stub).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
